docs {
  # Create a user

  Store users — customers and administrators. `password` is write-only: it is hashed with bcrypt and never returned. Users created here are ACTIVE immediately. The role is returned inline as `role: { id, name, code }`.

  The server fills `created` with an audit stamp (`client`, `server`, `serverDate`, `serverTime` in APP_TIMEZONE, `unixTime`, `user`, `role` from the token). `status`, `statusName`, `created`, `updated`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and any other undeclared key are ignored if sent. An optional top-level `time` (ISO string) is recorded as `created.client`.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Body (JSON)

  | Field | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `roleId` | integer | yes on create | Id of an existing role. |
  | `genderId` | integer | yes on create | Id of an existing gender. |
  | `documentTypeId` | integer | yes on create | Id of an existing document type. |
  | `name` | string | yes on create | 1–100 characters. |
  | `lastName` | string | yes on create | 1–100 characters. |
  | `email` | string | yes on create | Valid email, stored lower-case; unique. |
  | `password` | string | yes on create | 8–72 characters, at least one letter and one digit. Write-only. |
  | `document` | string \| null | no | Identity document number; unique; max 50. |
  | `phone` | string \| null | no | Max 30 characters. |
  | `address` | string \| null | no | Max 300 characters. |

  ## Responses

  ### 201 Created

    {
      "message": "User created",
      "data": {
        "id": 1,
        "roleId": 2,
        "genderId": 4,
        "documentTypeId": 1,
        "name": "Ada",
        "lastName": "Lovelace",
        "email": "ada@lpaecomms.test",
        "document": "PA1234567",
        "phone": "+61 400 000 000",
        "address": "1 Cavill Ave, Surfers Paradise QLD",
        "emailVerified": false,
        "session": null,
        "deletedAt": null,
        "role": {
          "id": 2,
          "name": "Customer",
          "code": "CUSTOMER"
        },
        "created": {
          "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
          "serverTime": "12:30:14",
          "unixTime": 1790476214,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "updated": null,
        "statusName": "ACTIVE",
        "status": 1,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
      },
      "pagination": null
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  A body field is missing or invalid; one `errors` entry per field. Also returned when a referenced id does not exist (`roleId`, `genderId`, `documentTypeId`).

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "roleId",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 409 Conflict — a unique field is already in use

  Unique fields: `email`, `document`. Soft-deleted records still hold their values.

    {
      "message": "A record with this email already exists.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "email",
          "message": "email is already in use."
        }
      ]
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
